  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. Tests pass (39/39) and `npm run arch` reports no new violations.\n\nI kept the old fields because billing-service and analytics-ingest read this event, and ARCH-4 says renames and removals have to go through deprecation. Dropping them now would break those consumers on their next message.\n\n- **Event:** `src/core/events.ts` emits `amountCents` and `createdAt` with the same values as `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The old fields are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check the new fields alongside the old ones.\n- **Not touched:** The `GET /orders/{id}` response and the `POST /orders` 201 response still use `totalCents` and `placedAt`. You only asked about the event, and ARCH-8 requires that response to stay backward compatible. Internal names are unchanged too.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new field names. After that, a follow-up change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can add a deprecation note to the README if that would help.",
